Below are ten exploratory SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows) that gradually build up to the final request.

```sql
-- 1. Description: List a few rows from the director_mapping table to see movie‑ID / director‑ID pairs.
SELECT *
FROM "director_mapping"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: List distinct director IDs that appear in director_mapping.
SELECT DISTINCT "name_id"
FROM "director_mapping"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Look at the names table to find the literal names that correspond to the IDs.
SELECT *
FROM "names"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Join director_mapping to names to view the first 20 directors and their movies.
SELECT dm."movie_id", dm."name_id", n."name"
FROM "director_mapping" AS dm
LEFT JOIN "names" AS n
  ON dm."name_id" = n."id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Inspect the movies table focusing on id and duration.
SELECT "id", "duration"
FROM "movies"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Inspect the ratings table – movie ID, average rating and total votes.
SELECT "movie_id", "avg_rating", "total_votes"
FROM "ratings"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: How many movies does each director have? (unordered, sample 20)
SELECT dm."name_id",
       COUNT(*) AS "movie_count"
FROM "director_mapping" AS dm
GROUP BY dm."name_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Aggregate duration information per director (average & total).
SELECT dm."name_id",
       ROUND(AVG(m."duration")) AS "avg_duration",
       SUM(m."duration")        AS "total_duration",
       COUNT(*)                 AS "movie_count"
FROM "director_mapping" AS dm
JOIN "movies" AS m
  ON m."id" = dm."movie_id"
GROUP BY dm."name_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Aggregate rating statistics per director.
SELECT dm."name_id",
       ROUND(AVG(r."avg_rating"), 2)          AS "avg_rating",
       SUM(r."total_votes")                  AS "total_votes",
       MIN(r."avg_rating")                   AS "min_rating",
       MAX(r."avg_rating")                   AS "max_rating",
       COUNT(r."avg_rating")                 AS "rated_titles"
FROM "director_mapping" AS dm
JOIN "ratings" AS r
  ON r."movie_id" = dm."movie_id"
GROUP BY dm."name_id"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: Final query – top 9 directors by movie count, with all requested metrics.
SELECT
    dm."name_id"                                       AS "director_id",
    n."name"                                           AS "director_name",
    COUNT(*)                                           AS "movie_count",
    ROUND(AVG(m."duration"))                           AS "avg_movie_duration",
    ROUND(AVG(r."avg_rating"), 2)                      AS "avg_rating",
    SUM(r."total_votes")                               AS "total_votes",
    MIN(r."avg_rating")                                AS "min_rating",
    MAX(r."avg_rating")                                AS "max_rating",
    SUM(m."duration")                                  AS "total_movie_duration"
FROM "director_mapping"  AS dm
JOIN "movies"            AS m ON m."id" = dm."movie_id"
JOIN "ratings"           AS r ON r."movie_id" = dm."movie_id"
JOIN "names"             AS n ON n."id"   = dm."name_id"
GROUP BY dm."name_id", n."name"
ORDER BY
    COUNT(*)            DESC,
    SUM(m."duration")   DESC
LIMIT 9;
```
